msgid "DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/minios-module-manager.1:12
msgid ""
"B<MiniOS Module Manager> is a GTK 3 interface for MiniOS module composition "
"and module creation.  It runs as the desktop user and delegates privileged "
"or filesystem-sensitive operations to MiniOS Tools through fixed argument "
"vectors."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/minios-module-manager.1:16
msgid ""
"The application has two primary workspaces: Modules and Create.  The Modules "
"workspace distinguishes the modules composing the running system from those "
"selected for the next boot."
msgstr ""

#. type: SH
#: en/minios-module-manager.1:16
#, no-wrap
msgid "MODULES"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: en/minios-module-manager.1:17
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<Running Now>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/minios-module-manager.1:22
msgid ""
"Shows the authoritative ordered runtime module composition reported by "
"MiniOS Tools. Runtime activation and deactivation are available only when "
"the mounted root union is AUFS."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: en/minios-module-manager.1:22
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<Next Boot>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/minios-module-manager.1:27
msgid ""
"Shows the authoritative ordered module composition selected by the current "
"MiniOS boot rules. User modules can be added to or removed from durable "
"module storage when MiniOS Tools reports that such storage is available."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/minios-module-manager.1:32
msgid ""
"Selecting a module opens read-only details. When its backing source file is "
"available, the details also show its SquashFS contents and allow extraction "
"to a new directory. Extraction is an explicit operation and never overwrites "
"an existing destination."
msgstr ""

#. type: SH
#: en/minios-module-manager.1:32
#, no-wrap
msgid "CREATE"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/minios-module-manager.1:36
msgid ""
"The Create workspace provides reviewed workflows for repository or local "
"Debian packages, installation scripts, an interactive chroot, existing "
"folders, and the current session changes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/minios-module-manager.1:39
msgid ""
"Every workflow separates configuration, review, execution, and result. "
"Creating a module does not activate it or add it to the next boot "
"automatically."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/minios-module-manager.1:45
msgid ""
"The interactive chroot uses an embedded VTE terminal and the protected "
"B<chroot2sb>(1)  prepare/shell/finish/cancel lifecycle. Current-session "
"capture uses cancellable B<savechanges>(1)  and its standard MiniOS "
"exclusion policy."
msgstr ""

#. type: SH
#: en/minios-module-manager.1:45
#, no-wrap
msgid "FILE OPENING AND DRAG AND DROP"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/minios-module-manager.1:48
msgid ""
"A local SquashFS module opened from the file manager is inspected only. It "
"is not activated and is not added to Next Boot."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/minios-module-manager.1:53
msgid ""
"Drag and drop is an input shortcut. One module opens inspection, Debian "
"package files populate Packages, a directory populates Folder, and another "
"regular file populates Installation Script. Dropping an item never executes "
"code or changes module composition by itself."
msgstr ""

#. type: SH
#: en/minios-module-manager.1:53
#, no-wrap
msgid "PRIVILEGES"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/minios-module-manager.1:56
msgid ""
"The graphical application is never run as root. Operations that require "
"privilege are started through pkexec and the relevant MiniOS Tools backend."
msgstr ""

